  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the development of Corneal Ulcer through a chain of indications that involve inflammatory conditions. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone is associated with Iritis and Uveitis, which are inflammatory eye diseases. These conditions are further linked to Fluorometholone and Medrysone, both of which are indicated to cause Corneal Ulcer. The shared pathway involves the use of corticosteroids in the treatment of inflammatory eye diseases, with Hydrocortisone and its analogs playing a role in the pathogenesis of corneal ulceration. The presence of multiple pathways linking Hydrocortisone to Corneal Ulcer highlights the potential for corticosteroid use in inflammatory conditions to contribute to ocular complications. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering corticosteroid use in the context of inflammatory diseases when evaluating the risk of corneal ulceration.",
